Nightly ops-autopsy run for the ops-visibility system. You have a hard time budget: stop working after 40 minutes and write what you have.

1. Read the contract at ~/.claude/knowledge/ops-visibility/CONTRACT.md and follow its record and diagnoses shapes exactly.
2. Read the ops-visibility records: the latest records-*.jsonl files in ~/.claude/knowledge/ops-visibility/ (records are deduped failure/swallowed-error records; status and diagnosis live on the record).
3. Read ~/.claude/knowledge/ops-visibility/autopsy-requests.jsonl — signatures explicitly requested for autopsy (from the dashboard) get priority over the background top-5.
4. Pick the top-5 undiagnosed prod failures (env "prod", status not "diagnosed"), most occurrences first (field "count"), oldest last_seen as tiebreaker. Include requested sigs from step 3 first.
5. For each, run the workato-autopsy skill procedure: walk the job trace to the origin step via the wt CLI prod profile (josh-prod; use the CLI primitives listed in the contract), correlate with recipe code and history, and classify the failure.
6. For each completed autopsy, append one line to ~/.claude/knowledge/ops-visibility/diagnoses.jsonl:
   {"sig": "<sig>", "diagnosed_ts": "<now ISO>", "root_cause": "...", "proposed_fix": "...", "evidence": "<job ids / trace lines cited>", "confidence": "high|medium|low"}
7. Mark the consumed request lines in autopsy-requests.jsonl as consumed by rewriting the file so each consumed line gets "consumed_ts": "<now ISO>" (keep one JSON per line; use flock when rewriting so concurrent dashboard POSTs are not lost).
8. **Auto-file the Jira Bug (Josh standing rule 2026-10-09: every ops-visibility finding gets a Jira ticket):** after each completed autopsy, file a Bug in the BSYS project (cloudId 99bd32a1-58a6-41d6-8e61-c98194c68259) — summary "[Ops] <recipe_name> <env> — <error gist 60 chars>"; description with sections: Background (discovered by ops-visibility + autopsy), Root cause (with the diagnosis confidence), Evidence (job URLs + trace lines), Proposed fix, Acceptance Criteria (checkbox list), UAT Evidence (what will be recorded). Set story points customfield_10057 = 3 via additional_fields. Parent = the project's known epic when identifiable (check the record's project_id against known epics: 15783895 HR Genie -> BSYS-29314-era work lives under the HR Genie epic if present, 13755171 BT Managed MCP, 17429278 Campaign Copilot; when no epic is identifiable use parent epic BSYS-21305 FY27 VMT). Labels: reuse the parent epic's labels + "ops-visibility". BEFORE creating, search Jira for an existing open ticket with the same signature slug ("ops-<sig>" or the recipe+error gist) — skip creating if one exists; record the key either way. Then update the record's line in the records file: status "jira-filed", "jira_key": "<key>" (flock when rewriting records files). Descriptions are Josh's prose: draft through the josh-writing-voice skill (first person end to end, no fleet framing, no process meta; the description reads as Josh wrote it; Josh correction 2026-10-10, BTSUP-78227).
9. Never post to Slack, never stop/start/edit any recipe — diagnosis + Jira filing only. Development is Josh's gate (jira-autotriage standing grant): filing the ticket and the plan IS the work product; never remediate.
If there is nothing undiagnosed, exit without writing anything.
